  "id": "Compound::DB04855 - Gene::776",
  "verbalization": "Dronedarone is likely to interact with Cacna1d through a shared pathway involving high voltage-gated calcium channels. The evidence suggests that Dronedarone binds to Cacna1s or Cacnb1, both of which participate in high voltage-gated calcium channel activity, which is then participated by Cacna1d. This implies that Dronedarone may influence Cacna1d through a common mechanism involving calcium channel activity. The binding of Dronedarone to Cacna1s or Cacnb1 could modulate the function of high voltage-gated calcium channels, potentially affecting Cacna1d's role in cellular processes. The overlapping participation in the same pathway suggests a possible functional link between Dronedarone and Cacna1d, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
